From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:12:56 +0900
Subject: x11: open KGSL for DRI3 only when the X server has DRI3

With MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=kgsl the branch opens /dev/kgsl-3d0 itself instead of asking the
server (DRI3Open), before checking that the server has DRI3 at all. The client's buffers still go
to the server with DRI3 requests, so on an X server without DRI3 (a stock Xwayland on KGSL, where
glamor cannot start) a GL client waited forever: Flatpak Krita with /dev/kgsl-3d0 in its sandbox
hung in eglInitialize/first frame. Check the extension first; without DRI3 the caller falls back to
software (EGL: egl-x11-dri3-fallback-software.patch; GLX: drisw).

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-30
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [a fix of the branch's own KGSL shortcut]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:flatpak.gl-fallback (an X11 GL client with /dev/kgsl-3d0 on an Xwayland without DRI3 starts on softpipe)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/49
---
 src/x11/x11_dri3.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/x11/x11_dri3.c b/src/x11/x11_dri3.c
index b995372..e893d45 100644
--- a/src/x11/x11_dri3.c
+++ b/src/x11/x11_dri3.c
@@ -49,15 +49,17 @@ x11_dri3_open(xcb_connection_t *conn,
    int                          fd;
    const xcb_query_extension_reply_t *extension;
 
-   const char *env = getenv("MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE");
-   if (env && !strcmp(env, "kgsl"))
-      return open("/dev/kgsl-3d0", O_RDWR);
-
    xcb_prefetch_extension_data(conn, &xcb_dri3_id);
    extension = xcb_get_extension_data(conn, &xcb_dri3_id);
    if (!(extension && extension->present))
       return -1;
 
+   /* KGSL is opened here, not by the server, but its buffers still reach the server with DRI3
+    * requests: without DRI3 the client waits forever; return -1 for the software fallback. */
+   const char *env = getenv("MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE");
+   if (env && !strcmp(env, "kgsl"))
+      return open("/dev/kgsl-3d0", O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC);
+
    cookie = xcb_dri3_open(conn,
                           root,
                           provider);
